NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"intent review"},{"type":"text","value":" shows which library skills and planning records need review after source changes. Completed reviews are remembered until their source or guidance changes again."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For the full maintainer pipeline, use "},{"type":"link","href":"./intent-maintainer","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"intent maintainer review"}]},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--base"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--json"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--record"},{"type":"text","value":". It uses the same source-review implementation and report format described here. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"intent maintainer check"},{"type":"text","value":" combines review with registration, skill validation, distribution, and generated-file checks. The standalone command remains available for review-only checks and generated workflow reminders."}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"local-install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"\":[[\"@tanstack/intent@latest\",\"review\",\"[dir]\",\"[--base\",\"<ref>]\",\"[--json]\",\"[--check]\",\"[--record\",\"<report.json>]\",\"[--github-review]\",\"[--package-label\",\"<label>]\"]]},\"mode\":\"local-install\"}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For the normal coding-agent workflow, run "},{"type":"link","href":"./intent-maintainer#setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"maintainer setup"}]},{"type":"text","value":" once. The installed guidance instructs the agent to review guidance and maintain the planning documents before handoff."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"quick-start","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Quick start"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"intent review"},{"type":"text","value":" from your library repository to see pending work."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ask your agent to review those items using the current source change. It updates the skills and planning record, then runs the relevant checks."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep the resulting "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".intent/review-state.json"},{"type":"text","value":" with the source, skills, and planning documents in your change."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"intent review --check"},{"type":"text","value":" to confirm that no unreviewed items remain."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A justified no-op is a completed review. Missing evidence remains pending."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"comparison-and-output","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Comparison and output"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Behavior"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[dir]"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Locate the Git working tree. The review covers that repository, including its packages."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--base <ref>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compare against an available Git commit or ref, such as the actual PR base."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--json"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Print the complete structured report for an agent or script."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--check"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Exit nonzero when review items remain."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"recording-and-reminders","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recording and reminders"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Behavior"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--record <report.json>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Record completed outcomes from an annotated JSON report."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--github-review"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Write "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"review-items.json"},{"type":"text","value":", a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pr-body.md"},{"type":"text","value":" reminder when needed, and GitHub step output/summary when configured."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--package-label <label>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set the library label in generated reminder items."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--record"},{"type":"text","value":" cannot be combined with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--base"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--json"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--check"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--github-review"},{"type":"text","value":" cannot be combined with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--record"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--json"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--check"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"behavior","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Behavior"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"what-appears-in-a-review","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What appears in a review"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Item"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why it appears"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What to do"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Skill ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skill"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No recorded review, changed source, or changed skill/reference content."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compare the guidance with the source and update it when needed."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Planning records ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"planning"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The domain map, spec, or tree needs initial review, or its source/skill evidence changed."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reconcile all three documents, preserving earlier decisions and remaining work."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unmapped change ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"source"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A changed file is outside declared skill sources and not an "},{"type":"link","href":"#ignored-paths","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ignored path"}]},{"type":"text","value":", or a skill was removed."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Decide whether existing guidance, a new skill, or an exclusion is appropriate."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An unmapped file does not automatically require a new skill. A planning review can be needed even when nobody edited the planning documents."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"comparison-scope","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Comparison scope"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Git and an initial commit are required. The default command is read-only."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Setting"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Comparison"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Explicit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--base"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The commit selected by that ref."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Existing review state"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The first recorded baseline, plus each item's recorded content hashes."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No review state"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each tracked skill uses the commit that introduced it to identify subsequent mapped-source changes. New skills still require an initial review; repository-wide unmapped changes use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"HEAD"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Items without a recorded review use their introducing commit even when repository review state exists, unless you pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--base"},{"type":"text","value":". Planning records use the commit that introduced their "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skill_tree.yaml"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The comparison includes committed changes since the base and staged, unstaged, and untracked files visible to Git. Renames appear as removals and additions. It reviews final working-tree content; a partially staged index is not separately certified."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recorded hashes detect later edits even when a review happened before a commit. The state retains hashes rather than earlier source text. Default review fails closed when its stored baseline is no longer available; it does not infer a replacement from rewritten history."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"recover-an-unavailable-baseline","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recover an unavailable baseline"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A squash merge, shallow clone, or history rewrite can remove the commit stored as the review baseline. Choose an available commit that covers the changes you intend to review, then create an explicit-base report:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"local-install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"\":[[\"@tanstack/intent@latest\",\"review\",\"--base\",\"<available-commit>\",\"--json\",\">\",\".intent/review.json\"]]},\"mode\":\"local-install\"}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Review and resolve every item in that report, then record it:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"local-install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"\":[[\"@tanstack/intent@latest\",\"review\",\"--record\",\".intent/review.json\"]]},\"mode\":\"local-install\"}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When the previous stored baseline is unavailable, recording this fully resolved explicit-base report adopts the report's base as the new durable baseline. An empty report can also adopt the new base because it records that the selected comparison has no pending items. A partial report, an omitted or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unresolved"},{"type":"text","value":" outcome, unresolved source or planning evidence, or a changed fingerprint cannot replace the missing baseline. When the stored baseline is still available, recording an explicit-base report does not replace it."}]},{"type":"callout","kind":"warning","title":"Select the recovery base deliberately","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The selected base sets the Git comparison boundary. Fetch missing history when possible. Otherwise choose a reachable commit old enough to include every intended change; a base that is too recent can omit earlier unreviewed changes."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"source-mappings","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source mappings"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Discovery covers first-party "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skills/**/SKILL.md"},{"type":"text","value":" files in the repository and its packages that "},{"type":"link","href":"#ignored-paths","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"review.ignore"}]},{"type":"text","value":" does not match, custom roots containing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"_artifacts/"},{"type":"text","value":", exact paths declared in the skill tree, and previously reviewed skill paths. An unrelated "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SKILL.md"},{"type":"text","value":" elsewhere does not automatically become a library skill. Review excludes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"node_modules"},{"type":"text","value":", even without a Git ignore rule."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source entry"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Resolution"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/request.ts"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Relative to the owning package, including skills in custom directories."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"owner/repository:src/request.ts"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Relative to the Git root; the repository identity must match the origin or root package metadata."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"src/**/*.ts"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Git glob syntax: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"*"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"?"},{"type":"text","value":", character classes, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"**"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Brace expansion and extglobs are unsupported. Ignored files, submodules, external source repositories, and symbolic links require manual review. Missing or unsupported mappings remain unresolved."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"ignored-paths","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ignored paths"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Files that Intent writes or that carry no library guidance do not appear as unmapped changes. The default list covers the agent instruction files ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AGENTS.md"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CLAUDE.md"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".cursorrules"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".github/copilot-instructions.md"},{"type":"text","value":"), "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".claude-plugin/**"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".cursor-plugin/**"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".github/workflows/check-skills.yml"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".intent/**"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"**/package.json"},{"type":"text","value":", and the lockfiles ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pnpm-lock.yaml"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"package-lock.json"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"npm-shrinkwrap.json"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"yarn.lock"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"bun.lock"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The list only stops these paths from surfacing as unmapped changes. A skill that lists one of them in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sources"},{"type":"text","value":" still tracks it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add repository-specific patterns under "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"review.ignore"},{"type":"text","value":" in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skill_tree.yaml"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"review:\n  ignore:\n    - \"docs/**\"\n    - \"examples/**/package.json\"","lang":"yaml"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Entries use the same Git glob syntax as source mappings. An entry that is not a non-empty string fails review with the path of the tree file."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skills/**/SKILL.md"},{"type":"text","value":" that matches "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"review.ignore"},{"type":"text","value":" is not a library skill: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maintainer setup"},{"type":"text","value":" does not register it, and review skips it unless the skill tree declares its path or the review state already records it. Use this for agent skills kept beside the library, such as the skills of a Claude Code plugin."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"required-planning-documents","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required planning documents"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The maintainer workflow keeps a cumulative record across batches:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Document"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Records"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"domain_map.yaml"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Domains, developer tasks, relationships, failure modes, and gaps."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skill_spec.md"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Readable coverage, maintainer decisions, batch history, and remaining work."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skill_tree.yaml"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Skill identities, paths, package placement, prerequisites, and source mappings."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Review finds existing planning locations from these filenames, including custom directories. Without one, installed maintainer guidance requires "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"_artifacts/"},{"type":"text","value":" at a monorepo root or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skills/_artifacts/"},{"type":"text","value":" for a standalone library. Previously recorded locations remain required if their files are deleted."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All three files must be present, nonempty, readable, and visible to Git. Each YAML document must contain an object with a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skills"},{"type":"text","value":" array. Missing or invalid records remain unresolved."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The planning snapshot includes the documents and the discovered skill/source evidence. Changes reopen planning review without reopening an otherwise unchanged individual skill. The check establishes file presence, YAML shape, and reviewed content hashes; the agent and maintainer still assess whether the written record is accurate and complete."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"record-a-completed-review","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Record a completed review"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"interactive-review","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interactive review"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For a human terminal, run the interactive command from the library repository:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"local-install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"\":[[\"@tanstack/intent@latest\",\"maintainer\",\"review\",\"--interactive\"]]},\"mode\":\"local-install\"}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Inspect each item's current guidance and changed files, choose an outcome, and supply the reason and actual evidence. The changes view compares tracked files with the displayed Git base and includes untracked content. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--base <available-commit>"},{"type":"text","value":" for a specific comparison. Edit and test guidance before starting; changes during review invalidate the affected outcomes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Choose "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Leave pending"}]},{"type":"text","value":" when more work is needed. Items with unresolved source mappings or planning problems cannot be completed. The final preview lists the proposed outcomes and evidence. Confirmation records through the same fingerprint checks as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--record"},{"type":"text","value":"; cancellation records nothing. Evidence text is stored, not executed or independently verified."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Interactive review requires a terminal outside CI and cannot be combined with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--json"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--record"},{"type":"text","value":". A zero exit status means the interaction completed, not that all review items were resolved. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"intent maintainer check --base <available-commit>"},{"type":"text","value":" as the read-only CI gate. JSON reports and the manual procedure below remain available to agents and scripts."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"record-all-pending-items","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Record all pending items"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After inspecting all pending items and running the relevant checks, record one conclusion in one command:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"local-install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"\":[[\"@tanstack/intent@latest\",\"maintainer\",\"review\",\"--unchanged\",\"\\\"Checked\",\"retries\",\"and\",\"cancellation\",\"against\",\"the\",\"updated\",\"implementation;\",\"the\",\"guidance\",\"remains\",\"accurate.\\\"\"],[\"@tanstack/intent@latest\",\"maintainer\",\"review\",\"--updated\",\"\\\"Updated\",\"the\",\"affected\",\"examples\",\"and\",\"planning\",\"records,\",\"then\",\"checked\",\"them\",\"against\",\"the\",\"source.\\\"\"]]},\"mode\":\"local-install\"}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Choose one command. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--unchanged"},{"type":"text","value":" records "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"no-change"},{"type":"text","value":"; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--updated"},{"type":"text","value":" records "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"updated"},{"type":"text","value":". The reason is required and applies to every pending item. Intent records each item's current changed paths and head revision as evidence and applies the same fingerprint and unresolved-problem checks as JSON recording. The command fails when nothing is pending or any item cannot be recorded. It does not assess the guidance or run the checks for you."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These flags belong to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maintainer review"},{"type":"text","value":", accept "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--base"},{"type":"text","value":", and cannot be combined with each other, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--json"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--record"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--interactive"},{"type":"text","value":". Use a JSON report when items need different conclusions or more detailed evidence."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"json-review","children":[{"type":"text","value":"JSON review"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The installed maintainer procedure handles these steps. For manual use:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Review the pending items, edit guidance and planning records as needed, and run the relevant checks."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Regenerate the report after those edits. Save it outside source paths, such as under "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".intent/"},{"type":"text","value":", which the maintainer commands create:"}]}]}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"local-install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"\":[[\"@tanstack/intent@latest\",\"review\",\"--json\",\">\",\".intent/review.json\"]]},\"mode\":\"local-install\"}"}},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":3,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Add an outcome, reason, and evidence to each item you completed. Preserve the report's identities, baseline, and fingerprints. The report's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recording"},{"type":"text","value":" block lists the accepted values."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Record the report and check remaining work:"}]}]}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"local-install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"\":[[\"@tanstack/intent@latest\",\"review\",\"--record\",\".intent/review.json\"],[\"@tanstack/intent@latest\",\"review\",\"--check\"]]},\"mode\":\"local-install\"}"}},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"outcomes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Outcomes"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Outcome"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Meaning"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Clears the item?"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"updated"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Guidance or planning records were corrected and checked."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Yes, with current fingerprints and resolved evidence."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"no-change"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The existing content was checked and remains accurate."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Yes, with a reason and evidence."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"out-of-scope"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A skill or source item is outside the reviewed guidance scope."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Yes, with a reason and evidence. Not accepted for planning records."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unresolved"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required evidence or a decision is still missing."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No outcome"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The item has not been reviewed."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For example, add these fields to an existing report item; this is not a complete report:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"{\n  \"outcome\": \"no-change\",\n  \"reason\": \"Only the internal cache changed; the documented retry bound and errors remain the same.\",\n  \"evidence\": [\"src/request.ts\", \"test/request.test.ts: passed\"]\n}","lang":"json"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For a planning item, the reason and evidence must cover all three documents. Preserve prior tasks, decisions, and future work when extending them with a new batch."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--record"},{"type":"text","value":" rejects a report that annotates none of its items. The error names the required fields and points to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"intent maintainer review --interactive"},{"type":"text","value":"; a report with zero items still records its baseline."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"saved-state","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Saved state"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--record"},{"type":"text","value":" writes "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".intent/review-state.json"},{"type":"text","value":" containing the baseline, source/guidance hashes, reviewed revision, outcomes, reasons, and evidence, creating the directory when it is missing. It does not commit, publish, or change skill versions. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".intent/"},{"type":"text","value":" is reserved for Intent's working files and is excluded from unmapped-change items: review state and working reports, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".intent/skill-distribution.json"},{"type":"text","value":" written by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maintainer sync"},{"type":"text","value":", and the temporary "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".intent/maintainer.lock"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".intent/review-state.json.lock"},{"type":"text","value":" that serialize writes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Identical recorded content suppresses repeat reminders. Later edits reopen review. The saved state does not replace the planning documents, execute evidence strings, or verify the truth of a recorded conclusion."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"default-and-json-output","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Default and JSON output"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text output shows the pending count and up to 20 items, with changed paths, unresolved problems, and the next step. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--json"},{"type":"text","value":" for the full report."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"JSON field"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Meaning"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"schemaVersion"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Report format version; currently "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"1"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"root"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"head"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"base"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Working-tree identity and compared Git revisions."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"recording"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Accepted "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outcomes"},{"type":"text","value":", the narrower "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"planningOutcomes"},{"type":"text","value":", the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"required"},{"type":"text","value":" fields ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outcome"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reason"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"evidence"},{"type":"text","value":"), and the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"command"},{"type":"text","value":" that records the report. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--record"},{"type":"text","value":" ignores this block."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"items"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pending skill, planning, and source review items."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Item "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"kind"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"path"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stable item identity, category, and location."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Item "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"changedFiles"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Paths changed since the relevant comparison. Can be empty for initial review."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Item "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"snapshot"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fingerprint"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Current content hashes and item fingerprint used when recording."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Item "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"problems"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unresolved evidence that prevents recording completion."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"automated-checks","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Automated checks"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The optional version 4 "},{"type":"link","href":"./intent-setup","children":[{"type":"text","value":"setup workflow"}]},{"type":"text","value":" connects review to PRs and releases:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Trigger"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pull request with maintainer guidance or review state"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"maintainer check --base <PR-base-sha>"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Release/manual run with review state"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"review --github-review"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Release/manual run without review state"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Existing "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"stale --github-review"},{"type":"text","value":" fallback"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This catches skipped review recording and missing planning documents. It does not run an authoring model in CI. Your coding agent handles the reminder using the same maintainer procedure."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"status-and-errors","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Status and errors"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Result"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Behavior or next step"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No pending items"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--check"},{"type":"text","value":" exits "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pending review"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--check"},{"type":"text","value":" exits nonzero; review and record the remaining items."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Missing, empty, or invalid planning document"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Restore or repair the record before recording completion."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source or guidance changed after the report"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Regenerate "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--json"},{"type":"text","value":" after editing; stale fingerprints are rejected."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Missing recorded baseline"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fetch the referenced history, or create and fully resolve an explicit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--base"},{"type":"text","value":" report to adopt a deliberate available baseline."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Missing or option-like explicit base"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass a reachable commit or ref; explicit bases remain strict and are never inferred."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Corrupt review state"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Restore or repair the state; Intent does not silently discard it."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Existing recording lock"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wait for the current recording. Remove the reported "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".intent/review-state.json.lock"},{"type":"text","value":" only after confirming no recording is running, then regenerate the report and retry."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Wrong working tree"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Regenerate the report in the repository being reviewed."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Git/setup failure"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Normal review exits nonzero. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"--github-review"},{"type":"text","value":" writes a failure reminder so the missing evidence stays visible."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"related","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Related"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../getting-started/quick-start-maintainers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Maintainer quick start"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./intent-install","children":[{"type":"text","value":"intent install"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./intent-validate","children":[{"type":"text","value":"intent validate"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./intent-stale","children":[{"type":"text","value":"intent stale"}]}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"quick-start","text":"Quick start","level":2},{"id":"options","text":"Options","level":2},{"id":"comparison-and-output","text":"Comparison and output","level":3},{"id":"recording-and-reminders","text":"Recording and reminders","level":3},{"id":"behavior","text":"Behavior","level":2},{"id":"what-appears-in-a-review","text":"What appears in a review","level":3},{"id":"comparison-scope","text":"Comparison scope","level":3},{"id":"recover-an-unavailable-baseline","text":"Recover an unavailable baseline","level":3},{"id":"source-mappings","text":"Source mappings","level":3},{"id":"ignored-paths","text":"Ignored paths","level":3},{"id":"required-planning-documents","text":"Required planning documents","level":3},{"id":"record-a-completed-review","text":"Record a completed review","level":2},{"id":"interactive-review","text":"Interactive review","level":3},{"id":"record-all-pending-items","text":"Record all pending items","level":3},{"id":"json-review","text":"JSON review","level":3},{"id":"outcomes","text":"Outcomes","level":3},{"id":"saved-state","text":"Saved state","level":3},{"id":"default-and-json-output","text":"Default and JSON output","level":2},{"id":"automated-checks","text":"Automated checks","level":2},{"id":"status-and-errors","text":"Status and errors","level":2},{"id":"related","text":"Related","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n`intent review` shows which library skills and planning records need review after source changes. Completed reviews are remembered until their source or guidance changes again.\n\nFor the full maintainer pipeline, use [`intent maintainer review`](./intent-maintainer) with `--base`, `--json`, or `--record`. It uses the same source-review implementation and report format described here. `intent maintainer check` combines review with registration, skill validation, distribution, and generated-file checks. The standalone command remains available for review-only checks and generated workflow reminders.\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"local-install\" -->\n\n```text\n@tanstack/intent@latest review [dir] [--base <ref>] [--json] [--check] [--record <report.json>] [--github-review] [--package-label <label>]\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nFor the normal coding-agent workflow, run [maintainer setup](./intent-maintainer#setup) once. The installed guidance instructs the agent to review guidance and maintain the planning documents before handoff.\n\n## Quick start\n\n1. Run `intent review` from your library repository to see pending work.\n2. Ask your agent to review those items using the current source change. It updates the skills and planning record, then runs the relevant checks.\n3. Keep the resulting `.intent/review-state.json` with the source, skills, and planning documents in your change.\n4. Run `intent review --check` to confirm that no unreviewed items remain.\n\nA justified no-op is a completed review. Missing evidence remains pending.\n\n## Options\n\n### Comparison and output\n\n| Option | Behavior |\n| --- | --- |\n| `[dir]` | Locate the Git working tree. The review covers that repository, including its packages. |\n| `--base <ref>` | Compare against an available Git commit or ref, such as the actual PR base. |\n| `--json` | Print the complete structured report for an agent or script. |\n| `--check` | Exit nonzero when review items remain. |\n\n### Recording and reminders\n\n| Option | Behavior |\n| --- | --- |\n| `--record <report.json>` | Record completed outcomes from an annotated JSON report. |\n| `--github-review` | Write `review-items.json`, a `pr-body.md` reminder when needed, and GitHub step output/summary when configured. |\n| `--package-label <label>` | Set the library label in generated reminder items. |\n\n`--record` cannot be combined with `--base`, `--json`, or `--check`. `--github-review` cannot be combined with `--record`, `--json`, or `--check`.\n\n## Behavior\n\n### What appears in a review\n\n| Item | Why it appears | What to do |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Skill (`skill`) | No recorded review, changed source, or changed skill/reference content. | Compare the guidance with the source and update it when needed. |\n| Planning records (`planning`) | The domain map, spec, or tree needs initial review, or its source/skill evidence changed. | Reconcile all three documents, preserving earlier decisions and remaining work. |\n| Unmapped change (`source`) | A changed file is outside declared skill sources and not an [ignored path](#ignored-paths), or a skill was removed. | Decide whether existing guidance, a new skill, or an exclusion is appropriate. |\n\nAn unmapped file does not automatically require a new skill. A planning review can be needed even when nobody edited the planning documents.\n\n### Comparison scope\n\nGit and an initial commit are required. The default command is read-only.\n\n| Setting | Comparison |\n| --- | --- |\n| Explicit `--base` | The commit selected by that ref. |\n| Existing review state | The first recorded baseline, plus each item's recorded content hashes. |\n| No review state | Each tracked skill uses the commit that introduced it to identify subsequent mapped-source changes. New skills still require an initial review; repository-wide unmapped changes use `HEAD`. |\n\nItems without a recorded review use their introducing commit even when repository review state exists, unless you pass `--base`. Planning records use the commit that introduced their `skill_tree.yaml`.\n\nThe comparison includes committed changes since the base and staged, unstaged, and untracked files visible to Git. Renames appear as removals and additions. It reviews final working-tree content; a partially staged index is not separately certified.\n\nRecorded hashes detect later edits even when a review happened before a commit. The state retains hashes rather than earlier source text. Default review fails closed when its stored baseline is no longer available; it does not infer a replacement from rewritten history.\n\n### Recover an unavailable baseline\n\nA squash merge, shallow clone, or history rewrite can remove the commit stored as the review baseline. Choose an available commit that covers the changes you intend to review, then create an explicit-base report:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"local-install\" -->\n\n```text\n@tanstack/intent@latest review --base <available-commit> --json > .intent/review.json\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nReview and resolve every item in that report, then record it:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"local-install\" -->\n\n@tanstack/intent@latest review --record .intent/review.json\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nWhen the previous stored baseline is unavailable, recording this fully resolved explicit-base report adopts the report's base as the new durable baseline. An empty report can also adopt the new base because it records that the selected comparison has no pending items. A partial report, an omitted or `unresolved` outcome, unresolved source or planning evidence, or a changed fingerprint cannot replace the missing baseline. When the stored baseline is still available, recording an explicit-base report does not replace it.\n\n> [!WARNING] Select the recovery base deliberately\n> The selected base sets the Git comparison boundary. Fetch missing history when possible. Otherwise choose a reachable commit old enough to include every intended change; a base that is too recent can omit earlier unreviewed changes.\n\n### Source mappings\n\nDiscovery covers first-party `skills/**/SKILL.md` files in the repository and its packages that [`review.ignore`](#ignored-paths) does not match, custom roots containing `_artifacts/`, exact paths declared in the skill tree, and previously reviewed skill paths. An unrelated `SKILL.md` elsewhere does not automatically become a library skill. Review excludes `node_modules`, even without a Git ignore rule.\n\n| Source entry | Resolution |\n| --- | --- |\n| `src/request.ts` | Relative to the owning package, including skills in custom directories. |\n| `owner/repository:src/request.ts` | Relative to the Git root; the repository identity must match the origin or root package metadata. |\n| `src/**/*.ts` | Git glob syntax: `*`, `?`, character classes, and `**`. |\n\nBrace expansion and extglobs are unsupported. Ignored files, submodules, external source repositories, and symbolic links require manual review. Missing or unsupported mappings remain unresolved.\n\n### Ignored paths\n\nFiles that Intent writes or that carry no library guidance do not appear as unmapped changes. The default list covers the agent instruction files (`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.cursorrules`, `.github/copilot-instructions.md`), `.claude-plugin/**`, `.cursor-plugin/**`, `.github/workflows/check-skills.yml`, `.intent/**`, `**/package.json`, and the lockfiles (`pnpm-lock.yaml`, `package-lock.json`, `npm-shrinkwrap.json`, `yarn.lock`, `bun.lock`).\n\nThe list only stops these paths from surfacing as unmapped changes. A skill that lists one of them in `sources` still tracks it.\n\nAdd repository-specific patterns under `review.ignore` in `skill_tree.yaml`:\n\n```yaml\nreview:\n  ignore:\n    - \"docs/**\"\n    - \"examples/**/package.json\"\n```\n\nEntries use the same Git glob syntax as source mappings. An entry that is not a non-empty string fails review with the path of the tree file.\n\nA `skills/**/SKILL.md` that matches `review.ignore` is not a library skill: `maintainer setup` does not register it, and review skips it unless the skill tree declares its path or the review state already records it. Use this for agent skills kept beside the library, such as the skills of a Claude Code plugin.\n\n### Required planning documents\n\nThe maintainer workflow keeps a cumulative record across batches:\n\n| Document | Records |\n| --- | --- |\n| `domain_map.yaml` | Domains, developer tasks, relationships, failure modes, and gaps. |\n| `skill_spec.md` | Readable coverage, maintainer decisions, batch history, and remaining work. |\n| `skill_tree.yaml` | Skill identities, paths, package placement, prerequisites, and source mappings. |\n\nReview finds existing planning locations from these filenames, including custom directories. Without one, installed maintainer guidance requires `_artifacts/` at a monorepo root or `skills/_artifacts/` for a standalone library. Previously recorded locations remain required if their files are deleted.\n\nAll three files must be present, nonempty, readable, and visible to Git. Each YAML document must contain an object with a `skills` array. Missing or invalid records remain unresolved.\n\nThe planning snapshot includes the documents and the discovered skill/source evidence. Changes reopen planning review without reopening an otherwise unchanged individual skill. The check establishes file presence, YAML shape, and reviewed content hashes; the agent and maintainer still assess whether the written record is accurate and complete.\n\n## Record a completed review\n\n### Interactive review\n\nFor a human terminal, run the interactive command from the library repository:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"local-install\" -->\n\n@tanstack/intent@latest maintainer review --interactive\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nInspect each item's current guidance and changed files, choose an outcome, and supply the reason and actual evidence. The changes view compares tracked files with the displayed Git base and includes untracked content. Use `--base <available-commit>` for a specific comparison. Edit and test guidance before starting; changes during review invalidate the affected outcomes.\n\nChoose **Leave pending** when more work is needed. Items with unresolved source mappings or planning problems cannot be completed. The final preview lists the proposed outcomes and evidence. Confirmation records through the same fingerprint checks as `--record`; cancellation records nothing. Evidence text is stored, not executed or independently verified.\n\nInteractive review requires a terminal outside CI and cannot be combined with `--json` or `--record`. A zero exit status means the interaction completed, not that all review items were resolved. Use `intent maintainer check --base <available-commit>` as the read-only CI gate. JSON reports and the manual procedure below remain available to agents and scripts.\n\n### Record all pending items\n\nAfter inspecting all pending items and running the relevant checks, record one conclusion in one command:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"local-install\" -->\n\n```text\n@tanstack/intent@latest maintainer review --unchanged \"Checked retries and cancellation against the updated implementation; the guidance remains accurate.\"\n@tanstack/intent@latest maintainer review --updated \"Updated the affected examples and planning records, then checked them against the source.\"\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nChoose one command. `--unchanged` records `no-change`; `--updated` records `updated`. The reason is required and applies to every pending item. Intent records each item's current changed paths and head revision as evidence and applies the same fingerprint and unresolved-problem checks as JSON recording. The command fails when nothing is pending or any item cannot be recorded. It does not assess the guidance or run the checks for you.\n\nThese flags belong to `maintainer review`, accept `--base`, and cannot be combined with each other, `--json`, `--record`, or `--interactive`. Use a JSON report when items need different conclusions or more detailed evidence.\n\n### JSON review\n\nThe installed maintainer procedure handles these steps. For manual use:\n\n1. Review the pending items, edit guidance and planning records as needed, and run the relevant checks.\n2. Regenerate the report after those edits. Save it outside source paths, such as under `.intent/`, which the maintainer commands create:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"local-install\" -->\n\n```text\n@tanstack/intent@latest review --json > .intent/review.json\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n3. Add an outcome, reason, and evidence to each item you completed. Preserve the report's identities, baseline, and fingerprints. The report's `recording` block lists the accepted values.\n4. Record the report and check remaining work:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"local-install\" -->\n\n@tanstack/intent@latest review --record .intent/review.json\n@tanstack/intent@latest review --check\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n### Outcomes\n\n| Outcome | Meaning | Clears the item? |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `updated` | Guidance or planning records were corrected and checked. | Yes, with current fingerprints and resolved evidence. |\n| `no-change` | The existing content was checked and remains accurate. | Yes, with a reason and evidence. |\n| `out-of-scope` | A skill or source item is outside the reviewed guidance scope. | Yes, with a reason and evidence. Not accepted for planning records. |\n| `unresolved` | Required evidence or a decision is still missing. | No. |\n| No outcome | The item has not been reviewed. | No. |\n\nFor example, add these fields to an existing report item; this is not a complete report:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"outcome\": \"no-change\",\n  \"reason\": \"Only the internal cache changed; the documented retry bound and errors remain the same.\",\n  \"evidence\": [\"src/request.ts\", \"test/request.test.ts: passed\"]\n}\n```\n\nFor a planning item, the reason and evidence must cover all three documents. Preserve prior tasks, decisions, and future work when extending them with a new batch.\n\n`--record` rejects a report that annotates none of its items. The error names the required fields and points to `intent maintainer review --interactive`; a report with zero items still records its baseline.\n\n### Saved state\n\n`--record` writes `.intent/review-state.json` containing the baseline, source/guidance hashes, reviewed revision, outcomes, reasons, and evidence, creating the directory when it is missing. It does not commit, publish, or change skill versions. `.intent/` is reserved for Intent's working files and is excluded from unmapped-change items: review state and working reports, `.intent/skill-distribution.json` written by `maintainer sync`, and the temporary `.intent/maintainer.lock` and `.intent/review-state.json.lock` that serialize writes.\n\nIdentical recorded content suppresses repeat reminders. Later edits reopen review. The saved state does not replace the planning documents, execute evidence strings, or verify the truth of a recorded conclusion.\n\n## Default and JSON output\n\nText output shows the pending count and up to 20 items, with changed paths, unresolved problems, and the next step. Use `--json` for the full report.\n\n| JSON field | Meaning |\n| --- | --- |\n| `schemaVersion` | Report format version; currently `1`. |\n| `root`, `head`, `base` | Working-tree identity and compared Git revisions. |\n| `recording` | Accepted `outcomes`, the narrower `planningOutcomes`, the `required` fields (`outcome`, `reason`, `evidence`), and the `command` that records the report. `--record` ignores this block. |\n| `items` | Pending skill, planning, and source review items. |\n| Item `id`, `kind`, `path` | Stable item identity, category, and location. |\n| Item `changedFiles` | Paths changed since the relevant comparison. Can be empty for initial review. |\n| Item `snapshot`, `fingerprint` | Current content hashes and item fingerprint used when recording. |\n| Item `problems` | Unresolved evidence that prevents recording completion. |\n\n## Automated checks\n\nThe optional version 4 [setup workflow](./intent-setup) connects review to PRs and releases:\n\n| Trigger | Check |\n| --- | --- |\n| Pull request with maintainer guidance or review state | `maintainer check --base <PR-base-sha>` |\n| Release/manual run with review state | `review --github-review` |\n| Release/manual run without review state | Existing `stale --github-review` fallback |\n\nThis catches skipped review recording and missing planning documents. It does not run an authoring model in CI. Your coding agent handles the reminder using the same maintainer procedure.\n\n## Status and errors\n\n| Result | Behavior or next step |\n| --- | --- |\n| No pending items | `--check` exits `0`. |\n| Pending review | `--check` exits nonzero; review and record the remaining items. |\n| Missing, empty, or invalid planning document | Restore or repair the record before recording completion. |\n| Source or guidance changed after the report | Regenerate `--json` after editing; stale fingerprints are rejected. |\n| Missing recorded baseline | Fetch the referenced history, or create and fully resolve an explicit `--base` report to adopt a deliberate available baseline. |\n| Missing or option-like explicit base | Pass a reachable commit or ref; explicit bases remain strict and are never inferred. |\n| Corrupt review state | Restore or repair the state; Intent does not silently discard it. |\n| Existing recording lock | Wait for the current recording. Remove the reported `.intent/review-state.json.lock` only after confirming no recording is running, then regenerate the report and retry. |\n| Wrong working tree | Regenerate the report in the repository being reviewed. |\n| Git/setup failure | Normal review exits nonzero. `--github-review` writes a failure reminder so the missing evidence stays visible. |\n\n## Related\n\n- [Maintainer quick start](../getting-started/quick-start-maintainers)\n- [intent install](./intent-install)\n- [intent validate](./intent-validate)\n- [intent stale](./intent-stale)\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: intent review\nid: intent-review\n---\n\n`intent review` shows which library skills and planning records need review after source changes. Completed reviews are remembered until their source or guidance changes again.\n\nFor the full maintainer pipeline, use [`intent maintainer review`](./intent-maintainer) with `--base`, `--json`, or `--record`. It uses the same source-review implementation and report format described here. `intent maintainer check` combines review with registration, skill validation, distribution, and generated-file checks. The standalone command remains available for review-only checks and generated workflow reminders.\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"local-install\" -->\n\n```text\n@tanstack/intent@latest review [dir] [--base <ref>] [--json] [--check] [--record <report.json>] [--github-review] [--package-label <label>]\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nFor the normal coding-agent workflow, run [maintainer setup](./intent-maintainer#setup) once. The installed guidance instructs the agent to review guidance and maintain the planning documents before handoff.\n\n## Quick start\n\n1. Run `intent review` from your library repository to see pending work.\n2. Ask your agent to review those items using the current source change. It updates the skills and planning record, then runs the relevant checks.\n3. Keep the resulting `.intent/review-state.json` with the source, skills, and planning documents in your change.\n4. Run `intent review --check` to confirm that no unreviewed items remain.\n\nA justified no-op is a completed review. Missing evidence remains pending.\n\n## Options\n\n### Comparison and output\n\n| Option | Behavior |\n| --- | --- |\n| `[dir]` | Locate the Git working tree. The review covers that repository, including its packages. |\n| `--base <ref>` | Compare against an available Git commit or ref, such as the actual PR base. |\n| `--json` | Print the complete structured report for an agent or script. |\n| `--check` | Exit nonzero when review items remain. |\n\n### Recording and reminders\n\n| Option | Behavior |\n| --- | --- |\n| `--record <report.json>` | Record completed outcomes from an annotated JSON report. |\n| `--github-review` | Write `review-items.json`, a `pr-body.md` reminder when needed, and GitHub step output/summary when configured. |\n| `--package-label <label>` | Set the library label in generated reminder items. |\n\n`--record` cannot be combined with `--base`, `--json`, or `--check`. `--github-review` cannot be combined with `--record`, `--json`, or `--check`.\n\n## Behavior\n\n### What appears in a review\n\n| Item | Why it appears | What to do |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Skill (`skill`) | No recorded review, changed source, or changed skill/reference content. | Compare the guidance with the source and update it when needed. |\n| Planning records (`planning`) | The domain map, spec, or tree needs initial review, or its source/skill evidence changed. | Reconcile all three documents, preserving earlier decisions and remaining work. |\n| Unmapped change (`source`) | A changed file is outside declared skill sources and not an [ignored path](#ignored-paths), or a skill was removed. | Decide whether existing guidance, a new skill, or an exclusion is appropriate. |\n\nAn unmapped file does not automatically require a new skill. A planning review can be needed even when nobody edited the planning documents.\n\n### Comparison scope\n\nGit and an initial commit are required. The default command is read-only.\n\n| Setting | Comparison |\n| --- | --- |\n| Explicit `--base` | The commit selected by that ref. |\n| Existing review state | The first recorded baseline, plus each item's recorded content hashes. |\n| No review state | Each tracked skill uses the commit that introduced it to identify subsequent mapped-source changes. New skills still require an initial review; repository-wide unmapped changes use `HEAD`. |\n\nItems without a recorded review use their introducing commit even when repository review state exists, unless you pass `--base`. Planning records use the commit that introduced their `skill_tree.yaml`.\n\nThe comparison includes committed changes since the base and staged, unstaged, and untracked files visible to Git. Renames appear as removals and additions. It reviews final working-tree content; a partially staged index is not separately certified.\n\nRecorded hashes detect later edits even when a review happened before a commit. The state retains hashes rather than earlier source text. Default review fails closed when its stored baseline is no longer available; it does not infer a replacement from rewritten history.\n\n### Recover an unavailable baseline\n\nA squash merge, shallow clone, or history rewrite can remove the commit stored as the review baseline. Choose an available commit that covers the changes you intend to review, then create an explicit-base report:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"local-install\" -->\n\n```text\n@tanstack/intent@latest review --base <available-commit> --json > .intent/review.json\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nReview and resolve every item in that report, then record it:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"local-install\" -->\n\n@tanstack/intent@latest review --record .intent/review.json\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nWhen the previous stored baseline is unavailable, recording this fully resolved explicit-base report adopts the report's base as the new durable baseline. An empty report can also adopt the new base because it records that the selected comparison has no pending items. A partial report, an omitted or `unresolved` outcome, unresolved source or planning evidence, or a changed fingerprint cannot replace the missing baseline. When the stored baseline is still available, recording an explicit-base report does not replace it.\n\n> [!WARNING] Select the recovery base deliberately\n> The selected base sets the Git comparison boundary. Fetch missing history when possible. Otherwise choose a reachable commit old enough to include every intended change; a base that is too recent can omit earlier unreviewed changes.\n\n### Source mappings\n\nDiscovery covers first-party `skills/**/SKILL.md` files in the repository and its packages that [`review.ignore`](#ignored-paths) does not match, custom roots containing `_artifacts/`, exact paths declared in the skill tree, and previously reviewed skill paths. An unrelated `SKILL.md` elsewhere does not automatically become a library skill. Review excludes `node_modules`, even without a Git ignore rule.\n\n| Source entry | Resolution |\n| --- | --- |\n| `src/request.ts` | Relative to the owning package, including skills in custom directories. |\n| `owner/repository:src/request.ts` | Relative to the Git root; the repository identity must match the origin or root package metadata. |\n| `src/**/*.ts` | Git glob syntax: `*`, `?`, character classes, and `**`. |\n\nBrace expansion and extglobs are unsupported. Ignored files, submodules, external source repositories, and symbolic links require manual review. Missing or unsupported mappings remain unresolved.\n\n### Ignored paths\n\nFiles that Intent writes or that carry no library guidance do not appear as unmapped changes. The default list covers the agent instruction files (`AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `.cursorrules`, `.github/copilot-instructions.md`), `.claude-plugin/**`, `.cursor-plugin/**`, `.github/workflows/check-skills.yml`, `.intent/**`, `**/package.json`, and the lockfiles (`pnpm-lock.yaml`, `package-lock.json`, `npm-shrinkwrap.json`, `yarn.lock`, `bun.lock`).\n\nThe list only stops these paths from surfacing as unmapped changes. A skill that lists one of them in `sources` still tracks it.\n\nAdd repository-specific patterns under `review.ignore` in `skill_tree.yaml`:\n\n```yaml\nreview:\n  ignore:\n    - \"docs/**\"\n    - \"examples/**/package.json\"\n```\n\nEntries use the same Git glob syntax as source mappings. An entry that is not a non-empty string fails review with the path of the tree file.\n\nA `skills/**/SKILL.md` that matches `review.ignore` is not a library skill: `maintainer setup` does not register it, and review skips it unless the skill tree declares its path or the review state already records it. Use this for agent skills kept beside the library, such as the skills of a Claude Code plugin.\n\n### Required planning documents\n\nThe maintainer workflow keeps a cumulative record across batches:\n\n| Document | Records |\n| --- | --- |\n| `domain_map.yaml` | Domains, developer tasks, relationships, failure modes, and gaps. |\n| `skill_spec.md` | Readable coverage, maintainer decisions, batch history, and remaining work. |\n| `skill_tree.yaml` | Skill identities, paths, package placement, prerequisites, and source mappings. |\n\nReview finds existing planning locations from these filenames, including custom directories. Without one, installed maintainer guidance requires `_artifacts/` at a monorepo root or `skills/_artifacts/` for a standalone library. Previously recorded locations remain required if their files are deleted.\n\nAll three files must be present, nonempty, readable, and visible to Git. Each YAML document must contain an object with a `skills` array. Missing or invalid records remain unresolved.\n\nThe planning snapshot includes the documents and the discovered skill/source evidence. Changes reopen planning review without reopening an otherwise unchanged individual skill. The check establishes file presence, YAML shape, and reviewed content hashes; the agent and maintainer still assess whether the written record is accurate and complete.\n\n## Record a completed review\n\n### Interactive review\n\nFor a human terminal, run the interactive command from the library repository:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"local-install\" -->\n\n@tanstack/intent@latest maintainer review --interactive\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nInspect each item's current guidance and changed files, choose an outcome, and supply the reason and actual evidence. The changes view compares tracked files with the displayed Git base and includes untracked content. Use `--base <available-commit>` for a specific comparison. Edit and test guidance before starting; changes during review invalidate the affected outcomes.\n\nChoose **Leave pending** when more work is needed. Items with unresolved source mappings or planning problems cannot be completed. The final preview lists the proposed outcomes and evidence. Confirmation records through the same fingerprint checks as `--record`; cancellation records nothing. Evidence text is stored, not executed or independently verified.\n\nInteractive review requires a terminal outside CI and cannot be combined with `--json` or `--record`. A zero exit status means the interaction completed, not that all review items were resolved. Use `intent maintainer check --base <available-commit>` as the read-only CI gate. JSON reports and the manual procedure below remain available to agents and scripts.\n\n### Record all pending items\n\nAfter inspecting all pending items and running the relevant checks, record one conclusion in one command:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"local-install\" -->\n\n```text\n@tanstack/intent@latest maintainer review --unchanged \"Checked retries and cancellation against the updated implementation; the guidance remains accurate.\"\n@tanstack/intent@latest maintainer review --updated \"Updated the affected examples and planning records, then checked them against the source.\"\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nChoose one command. `--unchanged` records `no-change`; `--updated` records `updated`. The reason is required and applies to every pending item. Intent records each item's current changed paths and head revision as evidence and applies the same fingerprint and unresolved-problem checks as JSON recording. The command fails when nothing is pending or any item cannot be recorded. It does not assess the guidance or run the checks for you.\n\nThese flags belong to `maintainer review`, accept `--base`, and cannot be combined with each other, `--json`, `--record`, or `--interactive`. Use a JSON report when items need different conclusions or more detailed evidence.\n\n### JSON review\n\nThe installed maintainer procedure handles these steps. For manual use:\n\n1. Review the pending items, edit guidance and planning records as needed, and run the relevant checks.\n2. Regenerate the report after those edits. Save it outside source paths, such as under `.intent/`, which the maintainer commands create:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"local-install\" -->\n\n```text\n@tanstack/intent@latest review --json > .intent/review.json\n```\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n3. Add an outcome, reason, and evidence to each item you completed. Preserve the report's identities, baseline, and fingerprints. The report's `recording` block lists the accepted values.\n4. Record the report and check remaining work:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"local-install\" -->\n\n@tanstack/intent@latest review --record .intent/review.json\n@tanstack/intent@latest review --check\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n### Outcomes\n\n| Outcome | Meaning | Clears the item? |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `updated` | Guidance or planning records were corrected and checked. | Yes, with current fingerprints and resolved evidence. |\n| `no-change` | The existing content was checked and remains accurate. | Yes, with a reason and evidence. |\n| `out-of-scope` | A skill or source item is outside the reviewed guidance scope. | Yes, with a reason and evidence. Not accepted for planning records. |\n| `unresolved` | Required evidence or a decision is still missing. | No. |\n| No outcome | The item has not been reviewed. | No. |\n\nFor example, add these fields to an existing report item; this is not a complete report:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"outcome\": \"no-change\",\n  \"reason\": \"Only the internal cache changed; the documented retry bound and errors remain the same.\",\n  \"evidence\": [\"src/request.ts\", \"test/request.test.ts: passed\"]\n}\n```\n\nFor a planning item, the reason and evidence must cover all three documents. Preserve prior tasks, decisions, and future work when extending them with a new batch.\n\n`--record` rejects a report that annotates none of its items. The error names the required fields and points to `intent maintainer review --interactive`; a report with zero items still records its baseline.\n\n### Saved state\n\n`--record` writes `.intent/review-state.json` containing the baseline, source/guidance hashes, reviewed revision, outcomes, reasons, and evidence, creating the directory when it is missing. It does not commit, publish, or change skill versions. `.intent/` is reserved for Intent's working files and is excluded from unmapped-change items: review state and working reports, `.intent/skill-distribution.json` written by `maintainer sync`, and the temporary `.intent/maintainer.lock` and `.intent/review-state.json.lock` that serialize writes.\n\nIdentical recorded content suppresses repeat reminders. Later edits reopen review. The saved state does not replace the planning documents, execute evidence strings, or verify the truth of a recorded conclusion.\n\n## Default and JSON output\n\nText output shows the pending count and up to 20 items, with changed paths, unresolved problems, and the next step. Use `--json` for the full report.\n\n| JSON field | Meaning |\n| --- | --- |\n| `schemaVersion` | Report format version; currently `1`. |\n| `root`, `head`, `base` | Working-tree identity and compared Git revisions. |\n| `recording` | Accepted `outcomes`, the narrower `planningOutcomes`, the `required` fields (`outcome`, `reason`, `evidence`), and the `command` that records the report. `--record` ignores this block. |\n| `items` | Pending skill, planning, and source review items. |\n| Item `id`, `kind`, `path` | Stable item identity, category, and location. |\n| Item `changedFiles` | Paths changed since the relevant comparison. Can be empty for initial review. |\n| Item `snapshot`, `fingerprint` | Current content hashes and item fingerprint used when recording. |\n| Item `problems` | Unresolved evidence that prevents recording completion. |\n\n## Automated checks\n\nThe optional version 4 [setup workflow](./intent-setup) connects review to PRs and releases:\n\n| Trigger | Check |\n| --- | --- |\n| Pull request with maintainer guidance or review state | `maintainer check --base <PR-base-sha>` |\n| Release/manual run with review state | `review --github-review` |\n| Release/manual run without review state | Existing `stale --github-review` fallback |\n\nThis catches skipped review recording and missing planning documents. It does not run an authoring model in CI. Your coding agent handles the reminder using the same maintainer procedure.\n\n## Status and errors\n\n| Result | Behavior or next step |\n| --- | --- |\n| No pending items | `--check` exits `0`. |\n| Pending review | `--check` exits nonzero; review and record the remaining items. |\n| Missing, empty, or invalid planning document | Restore or repair the record before recording completion. |\n| Source or guidance changed after the report | Regenerate `--json` after editing; stale fingerprints are rejected. |\n| Missing recorded baseline | Fetch the referenced history, or create and fully resolve an explicit `--base` report to adopt a deliberate available baseline. |\n| Missing or option-like explicit base | Pass a reachable commit or ref; explicit bases remain strict and are never inferred. |\n| Corrupt review state | Restore or repair the state; Intent does not silently discard it. |\n| Existing recording lock | Wait for the current recording. Remove the reported `.intent/review-state.json.lock` only after confirming no recording is running, then regenerate the report and retry. |\n| Wrong working tree | Regenerate the report in the repository being reviewed. |\n| Git/setup failure | Normal review exits nonzero. `--github-review` writes a failure reminder so the missing evidence stays visible. |\n\n## Related\n\n- [Maintainer quick start](../getting-started/quick-start-maintainers)\n- [intent install](./intent-install)\n- [intent validate](./intent-validate)\n- [intent stale](./intent-stale)\n"}
